  <event id="295">
      <start>12:30</start>
      <duration>00:30</duration>
      <room>K.4.401</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>OpenJDK on ARM: Quo vadis?</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Free Java Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk will cover progress with OpenJDK on ARM.  It&amp;#39;s&#xA;basically a progress report, but with some technical detail&#xA;about the changes needed for:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The new Hard FP ABI.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;ARM 7.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;#39;ll also discuss the issues that arise from the Java Memory Model&#xA;(also known as JSR 233.)  The talk will then be in two&#xA;halves, one part being very specific to Ed Nevill&amp;#39;s ARM Assembler&#xA;interpreter and JIT, and the other part will cover the ARM more&#xA;generally.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If there&amp;#39;s any time left I&amp;#39;ll also cover the upcoming ARM8&#xA;architecture.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2951">Andrew Haley</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>